      "message": "Does this need to get relocked when the CRC matches? Also lots of these return values are not actually getting checked. Refactoring these nested if-statements would make this easier to read; you could use label(s) to handle the cleanup (relocking)\n\n```\nint rv \u003d 0;\n\nrv \u003d rt3645_set_cfg_mode(dev, config_seq, len);\nif (rv) {\n    LOG_ERR(...);\n    return rv;\n}\n\n...\n\nif (rt3645_crc_check(dev) \u003d\u003d EC_SUCCESS) {\n    LOG_INF(\"No update needed\");\n    rv \u003d 0;\n    goto cleanup;\n}\n\nrv \u003d rt3645_apply_update_data(dev);\nif (rv) {\n    LOG_ERR(...)\n    goto cleanup;\n}\n\n... further update steps ...\n\ncleanup:\nint lock_rv \u003d rt3645_lock_nvm(dev);\nif(lock_rv) {\n    LOG_ERR(...);\n    return lock_rv;\n}\n\nreturn rv;\n```",
